`pipeline_refactored.py` is on disk, compiles clean, and produces the same `report.html` output. Here's what changed and why:

| Concern | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Credentials / paths | Hardcoded at top of file | `os.environ.get("KEY", "default")` |
| SQL injection | `"INSERT INTO errors VALUES ('%s', '%s', %d')" % (…)` | `cur.execute("INSERT INTO errors VALUES (?, ?, ?)", (…))` |
| Structure | One `proc_data()` function | `extract()` → `transform()` → `load()` + `generate_report()` |
| Log parsing | `line.split(" ")` chains, fragile `in "User"` checks | Compiled regex at module level (`_RE_LOG`, `_RE_USER`, `_RE_API`) |
| Types | None | TypedDict for each record shape + inline annotations |
| Docstrings | None | Per-function descriptions with Args / Returns |
